A||N||6||Greg Piet||3.1 longblocks for sale????||||1||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||01-19-2000||03:40 AM||||I am pretty sure my 2.8 gave up the ghost, so im gonna have to do some serious engine work.  Since I dont have the facilities to do it myself it will go to my local fiero mechanic.  I was thinking i would likely have to replace the motor at minimum with a shortblock.  Can somebody tell me if anyone sells the 3.1 longblocks, and if there is any ECM changes necessary.  If it is a straight drop in I think I'll have the mechanic do that but I need to know of some places that sell a 3.1.  I am so disturbed that my little fiero is ill a am preoccupied about that above all else.  Any info for this would be greatly appreciated. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||01-19-2000||06:44 AM||||I got a Grooms 2.8L long block from Ed Parks at the Fiero Factory (fierofactory@juno.com or (256) 420-5391) and am very pleased.  They also sell a 3.1 and a 3.4 all with warranties.<BR>I think a 3.1 is plug n play with no ECM mods required.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||01-19-2000||12:03 PM||||You have to make sure you ask for the correct 3.1 engine. If you get one that is used in, let's say a Corsica, then the pistons will be the wrong ones for our cast iron heads, but the right ones for the aluminum heads. I know for sure that the early 90's GM minivans had the cast iron headed 3.1 engines. If you get one of these, it should be a direct bolt-in if you use the Fiero intake, pulleys, belts, and accessories. The cam is very mild on these engines, so if you want any performance you may consider swapping in a better cam.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||01-19-2000||03:23 PM||||This is a little off-topic, but I was wondering if anybody has the specs for the 3.1 V6 that came in the 95 Chevy Lumina.  My friend just got one of those and it has some balls...  e-mail anything to me.  TIA<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierosound||01-19-2000||05:04 PM||||This auto wrecker in the sounth-easter US has GM V6 long block engines with variuos mileage for $350-450.  You may want to see if they have anything you can use.<P> <A HREF="http://www.tacreationsusa.com/v6.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tacreationsusa.com/v6.htm</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000005||WKDFIRO||01-20-2000||08:28 PM||||Why go 3.1 when you can have a 3.4? Check out the threads about the 3.4. It will use the 2.8 harness with the 2.8 ECM with no problems. The ECMs are not as finicky as you would think.<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 01-20-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000006||fieroshop||01-20-2000||09:07 PM||||I highly recomend going to a 3.4 That is what I'll be doing the most of as soon as I get my template so that I can drill and tap the bolt holes for the starter on th e opposite side.||||reg||7
